  "content": "<p>Check your understanding of this lesson. Your answers aren't recorded.</p>\n<multiple-choice question=\"What is retopology?\" single-option=\"\" randomize=\"\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"Building a clean, lower-polygon mesh over a detailed sculpt\" data-correct=\"true\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"Adding subdivision levels to a sculpt\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"Painting textures onto a model\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"Rigging a character for animation\">\n</multiple-choice>\n<true-false-question question=\"It's good practice to establish large forms at low subdivision levels before adding fine detail.\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"True\" data-correct=\"true\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"False\">\n</true-false-question>\n<self-check title=\"Think it through\">\n  <p slot=\"question\">Why might you bake the details of a high-resolution sculpt into a normal map?</p>\n  <p>So a lower-polygon mesh that can be animated or used in real time keeps the look of the fine detail, without the cost of the sculpt's millions of polygons.</p>\n</self-check>\n"
